.IX Title "Clownfish::Blob 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Blob 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Blob \- Immutable buffer holding arbitrary bytes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $blob = Clownfish::Blob\->new($byte_string);
\&    my $byte_string = $blob\->to_perl;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $blob = Clownfish::Blob\->new($byte_string);
.Ve
.PP
Create a Blob containing the passed-in bytes.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $blob\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of bytes held by the Blob.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $blob\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one Blob is less than, equal to, or greater than
another.  The byte contents of the Blobs are compared
lexicographically.  Throws an exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is not a Blob.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the Blobs are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is less
than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $blob\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Blob isa Clownfish::Obj.
